WEBVTT

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.720
Glad to see you're still with us.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.600
If you'd died, you'd just need
your fare to cross the River Styx.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.680
Yeah.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.060
Sometimes, God seems to have my back.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.070
They must've asked God to
keep me away for just a bit longer.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:48.280
You know?

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:18.930
MEGALOBOX 2

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.960
Mio! Just wait, damn it!

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.090
Mio!

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:35.840
Mio!

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:38.760
I burned it down.

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:44.850
I'm gonna get kicked out anyway,
so I'll save you the trouble.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:50.360
So you're the one who told them about Joe.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.530
Only cowards conceal their names.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.450
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?!

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:55.820
Because of you--

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.530
Because of me?

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:00.030
You're the one who brought me into
this messed-up country, Mom!

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.290
I would've been better off dying

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:06.120
where I was born than
living in this shitty life!

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:16.930
Mio, don't talk about
dying so lightly like that.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:20.050
I'm not worried about the fire. So--

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:22.720
Get a friggin' clue, old man.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.640
You keep dreamin' when you know
none of that shit's gonna come true.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.900
Hey, you never know.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.650
It's your fault that your son died!

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:38.410
It's all your fault that Pops died!

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.200
Mio!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.870
How can you say something like that?!

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.270
Don't even try to stop me.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:09.900
I don't plan to.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:13.190
But if you leave now, you'll regret
it the rest of your life.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:16.610
This never would've happened
if you hadn't shown up.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.740
If only you hadn't stolen my ride...

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:25.870
Why don't you stick around
to see how this ends?

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:29.460
This ended a long time ago.
Everything did.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:41.090
Hey, Carlo.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:44.300
You're not giving your Mom
too much trouble, are ya?

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:49.100
I can feel myself
questioning things again.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.100
The fact that I left our
homeland with you,

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:55.190
and the fact that I'm trying
to rebuild a new home here...

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:05.280
Carlo, I met your old man here
and I'm still alive somehow.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.490
Thanks.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:11.040
I told you to wait in the car.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.590
If I left you alone now, I'm clearly
not meant to be your second.

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:21.090
If you feel weak in the knees,
I'll be there to give you a gentle push.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:27.010
I'm not the only one who wants to see
your dream come true anymore.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.640
Once someone dies, you can't
do anything for them.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.560
I'd always regretted that.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.820
You should go back to your own home.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:41.110
Even if you aren't welcomed back.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.200
We should get going.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:06:00.300
You always do that right before a match.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.800
It's a good luck charm from my homeland.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:06.430
"I hope I can come back safe."

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:07.640
Let's go.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:21.360
This won't do, Mr. Hikawa.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.610
I won't tell you how to do things,

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.530
but arson is crossing the line.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.330
Tell me about it.

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:32.450
Kids these days don't know how
to hold back. Terrifying, really.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.620
That being said,

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.130
as soon as those
immigrants leave that area

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:44.680
that land will be sold to me.
That was the deal, wasn't it?

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:46.220
<i>If </i>they leave.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:52.180
Not to worry. There's no way my
Mamiya will lose to that old fogey.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:55.190
I'm honestly fine with
however this turns out.

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:59.980
Whether it's you or the
immigrants that obtain that land.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:06.610
I will be cheering you
on though... in private.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:19.750
Hmph. Who does he think he is?

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:24.340
It would seem that our wittle friend has
never gotten into a fist fight before.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:30.850
Who will be going to Hell tonight?

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:35.430
Even though those immigrants
took our jobs and our pride,

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:38.980
our savior has come!

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:45.860
From Mans Mans World, Crazy Mamiya!

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:51.410
The two who have survived the tournament
will finally be clashing tonight!

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:57.750
Who will be victorious and take home that
cash prize to change their lives forever?

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:06.420
Kick his ass, Mamiya!

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:10.510
If you've got a problem, go back
home to your own country.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:14.890
Apparently, they don't teach you to
respect your elders in this country.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:18.640
Just because you almost look human
doesn't mean you get to speak like one.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.980
Calm down, Chief!

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:31.490
If you ask me, you're far
crazier than he'll ever be.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:36.950
Your heart may be crazy but keep
your head cool. Now breathe.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:52.510
You pathetic stray with nowhere to go...

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.260
--Hey! Stop him!
--Hey! That's cheating!

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.140
He can't punch him in the
back of the head like that!

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:04.610
Due to an illegal move,
Chief will face a deduction.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:04.610
Cheater!

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.230
Can't immigrants win without cheating?

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:12.820
Come on.

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:14.240
Don't step in.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.700
He can't keep up with your jabs.
Keep your distance!

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:21.420
Just how cowardly are you...

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.000
...and your people?

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:36.930
And he's down!

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:38.520
One!

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.100
Two!

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.810
Three!

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:43.520
Four!

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.270
Five!

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.070
Six!

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:48.860
Seven!

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:50.070
Eight!

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:02.460
Looks like Joe's right.
I am the crazy one here.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:05.630
Looks like I became a grumpy
old man because of my age.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.750
Just means you're still in your prime.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:15.050
You're coming back safe, aren't you?

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:21.640
You have somewhere to come home to.
Just concentrate on that.

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:44.870
You've got some balls hitchhiking
in these crazy times, kid.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:47.920
But I'm sure you have your reasons.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:51.840
People are free to choose
where they live or die.

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:05.890
Just can't let go, can you?

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:11.190
You're the one who left your homeland,
but you're still praying to some birds.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:15.070
Hell, I'd say that's quite a deal
if it makes my dream come true.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:16.950
Sure is convenient.

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:18.530
When your dream doesn't come true,

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.490
you can just blame God anyway.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:24.410
Hummingbirds aren't God's messengers.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.210
They symbolize our love for our homeland.

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.420
When you lose your way,

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:32.760
they remind us that we have
a place to come back home to.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:36.380
Listen to those empty words.
Okay, has-been.

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:43.350
Drop me off at the next rest stop.

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:47.190
You must've read my mind.
Let's go take a piss.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.150
Don't get the wrong idea, old man.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:55.900
G-Got it, kid. No need
to get so worked up.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:57.860
Come on, now...

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.240
Chief, don't back down!

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:04.700
Hit him from the side!

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:09.500
There you go! Don't hit him straight on!

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.460
That's it, Chief!

00:12:10.460 --> 00:12:12.130
Now kick his ass!

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:15.340
And he's down!

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:17.670
One!

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.340
Two!

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:21.010
Three!

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.810
Four!

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:24.260
Five!

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:38.150
Chief!

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:41.990
Due to a foul by Mamiya,
both fighters are now tied.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.450
Cheater!

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:41.990
You cheating bastard!

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:43.200
Chief!

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.460
It's over, old man.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:56.340
We're just getting started, punk.

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:22.240
Look, Chief.

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.740
He's at the end of his rope.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:26.540
The next round's gonna decide the winner.

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:33.790
Chief?

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.500
Hey, Joe.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:40.170
Am I shining like you did back then?

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:44.720
I know you hear those voices.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:48.680
Chief! Chief! Chief! Chief! Chief! Chief!

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:52.770
Chief! Chief! Chief! Chief...!

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:03.990
Joe.

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:07.950
If I win, don't try to drown out
what you're heart's tellin' ya.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:12.210
You know exactly what your heart desires.

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:16.380
It's a promise.

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:32.810
Excellent.

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:39.360
Carlo... are you watching?

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:40.570
Chief!

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.460
He's down!

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.960
One!

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:00.630
Two!

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:02.420
Three!

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.130
Four!

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:05.720
Five!

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:07.510
Six!

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:09.260
Seven!

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:10.850
Eight!

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:12.680
Nine!

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:13.890
Ten!

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:20.070
With a KO in the fifth round,
the winner is Chief!

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:25.950
Shit!

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:30.330
Hey! Go catch them!

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:33.040
What do you think you're here for?!

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:33.910
L-Let's go!

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:34.660
Don't just stand there!

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.120
Y-Yes, sir!

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:39.750
Quit dawdling! Go!

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:43.590
The one who dominated this tournament
and came out the champion

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:46.970
is the Real Boxer, Chief!

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.360
Cheers!

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:07.950
Come on, Marla.
At least let me have one drink.

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:12.080
You're just gonna have to
settle with this tonight.

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:16.750
Well, in return...

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.130
I need you to look after this.

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:27.170
I've been saving this up for a while.
I always hated doing messy paperwork.

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:34.430
I'll lock it up in my safe.

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:39.900
This is all thanks to you.

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:43.190
This isn't my victory.

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:45.480
You won because you believed in yourself.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.740
Dreams change people.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:53.080
Not just the dreamers.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:56.450
They pull in those around them,
and change them, as well.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:04.550
Joe, I'm going to continue dreaming
this dream that you showed me.

00:17:04.550 --> 00:17:08.470
So I want you to fulfill
your promise to me.

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:13.470
Yeah. I'm done runnin'.

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:20.640
What do you mean you're not
gonna hang with us anymore?

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:24.570
We only hung out with you
because we felt sorry for you.

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:25.480
Right?

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:27.400
Uh, yeah.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.360
I'm done.

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:32.820
I'm done doing awful things just
because I don't wanna be alone.

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:35.330
You know you had fun, too!

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:37.870
Yeah. Now, I can definitely tell

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:41.670
just how much of a pathetic loser I was.

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:46.090
I can't erase the past or act
like it never happened...

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:51.760
...but I'm going to continue living here.

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:53.930
Don't go acting like a
goody two-shoes now.

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:56.010
Go, on. Tell him, Bertie!

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:03.060
Do something about that haircut.
You look terrible.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.440
Y-Yeah.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:09.690
Huh? What? Wait, Takubon!

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:11.740
That dude's a traitor!

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:17.120
What the hell? Wait up, man!

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:22.790
What a nice breeze.

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:25.960
I'm thinking about leaving
tomorrow morning.

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:28.300
Make sure it's after you have
some of Marla's breakfast.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:29.380
Yeah.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.470
Say, Joe.

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:38.220
I'm scared to fall asleep.

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:45.100
I'm scared I'm gonna wake up and
find out everything was just a dream.

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:53.650
This is far enough. Tell everyone
I'm gonna head to bed.

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:55.740
Thanks, Chief.

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:06.380
You're my family, too. That's why
we helped each other out.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.210
Yeah.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:12.050
Well, see you tomorrow.

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:13.260
Yeah.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:20.430
You'll always be our champion.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:28.190
I wanna get in that ring
with you again someday.

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:30.270
For real, next time.

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:34.990
What'd you do to your hair?

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:36.240
Shove it.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:53.010
Good night.

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:07.810
Breakfast's ready.

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:10.110
I'm gonna go get Chief,
so you can go ahead.

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:11.320
Sure.

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:14.610
You really went all out this morning.

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:18.820
Both you and Chief need your energy.

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:21.530
This is what truly makes a man.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:25.580
This soup's my recipe
full of garlic and--

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:26.870
Mom!

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:35.710
Why...?

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:13.540
Chief once to me...

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:17.050
...that hummingbirds aren't
God's messengers.

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:19.930
They symbolize our love for our homeland.

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:22.260
When you lose your way,

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:26.810
they remind us that we have
a place to come back home to.

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:33.150
This Gear is a symbol of
everything Chief believed in.

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:35.690
And that's why you should have it.

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:41.200
Mom wanted to keep the gloves here.

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:41.200
Yes. Thank you very much.

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:45.160
But we want you to have this Gear.

00:21:45.160 --> 00:21:49.330
Because even if we don't have it, I'll be
the one to carry on Chief's legacy.

00:21:52.670 --> 00:21:54.750
I'll take good care of it.

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:57.550
<i>Mi casa es su casa.</i>

00:21:57.550 --> 00:22:00.340
Looks like this land is now legally ours.

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:04.010
All thanks to the money Chief left for us.

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:06.140
I'm gonna let everyone know!

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:13.270
Ready, and...

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:16.520
Yay!

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:20.900
What are you going to do now?
You know you're welcome to stay here.

00:22:23.030 --> 00:22:25.370
I have somewhere I have to get home to.

00:22:26.620 --> 00:22:30.450
I promised him that I
wouldn't run away anymore.
